12:23.534 --> 12:26.203
<i>I was home doing
what girls did at the time...</i>

12:26.204 --> 12:28.413
<i>Looking at pictures of John Elway.</i>

12:28.414 --> 12:31.541
My horse-toothed dreamboat.

12:31.542 --> 12:33.502
Denver looks beautiful.

12:33.503 --> 12:36.755
Peter?! How could you?!

12:36.756 --> 12:39.842
<i>My heart shattered the moment I saw it.</i>

12:41.511 --> 12:45.639
<i>I took your father's mixtape
and hucked it into the ocean.</i>

12:45.640 --> 12:49.351
<i>Right then and there, I vowed
I would never see him again.</i>

12:50.436 --> 12:52.159
She said "wood."

12:53.231 --> 12:54.815
That was cool.

12:54.816 --> 12:56.941
Yeah. Wood! Wood!

12:56.942 --> 12:59.027
You're right! Wood.

13:16.129 --> 13:19.172
Daddy, tell us more
about the black '90s.

13:19.173 --> 13:22.154
Well, Magic Johnson got AIDS,
and I was like, "What?!"

13:22.155 --> 13:24.845
But then, he came back the
next season and scored 30 points

13:24.846 --> 13:27.222
in a game where no one would touch him.

13:27.223 --> 13:30.058
And he caught it through
heterosexual sex contact?

13:30.059 --> 13:32.269
<i>Well, that is magic.</i>

13:32.270 --> 13:34.563
Terrific. Thank you, Cleveland.

13:34.564 --> 13:36.857
And thank you
to the entire Brown family,

13:36.858 --> 13:38.859
whose last name escapes me
at the moment.

13:38.860 --> 13:40.569
Terrific.

13:40.570 --> 13:41.862
Thanks, Dad.

13:41.863 --> 13:43.280
Now back to your story.

13:43.281 --> 13:45.407
I had just lost the love of my life.

13:45.408 --> 13:47.576
So as a way to forget my pain,

13:47.577 --> 13:51.146
I threw myself into
a dot-com startup with Quagmire.

13:51.147 --> 13:53.582
<i>We were two ambitious
young entrepreneurs</i>

13:53.583 --> 13:55.625
<i>at the height of the dot-com bubble.</i>

13:55.626 --> 13:58.263
Oogle? Goo goo?

13:58.264 --> 14:00.714
Gah-gah goo? Gee-gee goo? Go... go go?

14:00.715 --> 14:03.050
Keep saying baby words, Peter.
You're onto something.

14:03.051 --> 14:04.593
We're close. We're circling it!

14:04.594 --> 14:07.763
Goo-goo gah-gah? Oo... oogle?
Ooh eee ooh ah ah?

14:07.764 --> 14:10.140
<i>Moments late, we'd found
a business idea destined</i>

14:10.141 --> 14:13.518
<i>to change the tech world
forever: Googoogle.</i>

14:13.519 --> 14:16.313
<i>A search engine for all
the info on the Goo Goo Dolls.</i>

14:16.314 --> 14:19.608
People are always gonna need
information about them!

14:19.609 --> 14:21.068
<i>We were on our way.</i>

14:21.069 --> 14:22.736
<i>We rented office space,</i>

14:22.737 --> 14:25.614
<i>and watching it gave us
the idea to rent office space.</i>

14:25.615 --> 14:27.574
<i>Lumbergh.</i>

14:29.577 --> 14:33.246
Uh, clearly,
we hadn't discussed the, uh,

14:33.247 --> 14:34.831
<i>tone of our work environment.</i>

14:34.832 --> 14:36.636
I should say we haven't.

14:36.637 --> 14:38.668
I thought this was
to be a place of business.

14:38.669 --> 14:40.462
<i>We got over our initial differences,</i>

14:40.463 --> 14:42.297
<i>and then spent the rest of the day doing</i>

14:42.298 --> 14:44.091
<i>what everybody did in the '90s...</i>

14:44.092 --> 14:47.094
<i>Debating what was better...
Forrest Gump or Pulp Fiction.</i>

14:47.095 --> 14:48.970
<i>Forrest Gump is ridiculous!</i>

14:48.971 --> 14:52.099
One guy does what he's told all
the time and makes millions.

14:52.100 --> 14:55.477
But a girl goes off, tries to be
different, gets AIDS, and dies!

14:55.478 --> 14:58.313
I find your argument shallow
and pedantic.

14:58.314 --> 14:59.648
<i>I didn't see either one.</i>

14:59.649 --> 15:01.483
<i>I saw Ace Ventura 50 times.</i>

15:01.484 --> 15:03.777
<i>Laughed so hard, I crapped
myself in the theater.</i>

15:03.778 --> 15:05.112
<i>Just thinking about it now makes me...</i>

15:06.155 --> 15:07.239
<i>Ow!</i>

15:07.240 --> 15:09.157
<i>Meanwhile, my wedding plans</i>

15:09.158 --> 15:10.742
<i>with Tom Tucker were back on.</i>

15:10.743 --> 15:12.494
Are you ready? I can't believe

15:12.495 --> 15:14.329
the wedding is just two scenes away.

15:14.330 --> 15:16.190
What's wrong, sweetie?

15:16.191 --> 15:18.902
I guess I'm just not sure
if I'm doing the right thing.

15:18.903 --> 15:20.460
What if this is a mistake?

15:20.461 --> 15:22.963
Trust me, you're doing the right
thing. It's gonna be great.

15:22.964 --> 15:24.965
Now, listen, we don't have too
much time before the wedding,

15:24.966 --> 15:26.508
so I want to go over something

15:26.509 --> 15:27.968
regarding the father-daughter dance.

15:27.969 --> 15:31.138
It goes, "Dallah-hollah
wallah-ballah-dallah Macarena,

15:31.139 --> 15:33.181
wakka-lakka-chakka-hakka-bakka
Macarena."

15:33.182 --> 15:34.683
Daddy, I don't think

15:34.684 --> 15:36.852
"The Macarena" is
the best father-daughter dance.

15:36.853 --> 15:39.354
Well, how about another song
from the '90s?

15:39.355 --> 15:42.732
<i>Casey would waltz
with the strawberry blonde</i>

15:42.733 --> 15:46.653
<i>And the band played on...</i>

15:46.654 --> 15:48.780
What? Wrong '90s?

15:49.991 --> 15:51.533
<i>Like everything stupid</i>

15:51.534 --> 15:53.535
<i>in the '90s, Googoogle took off.</i>

15:53.536 --> 15:56.830
<i>We celebrated in grand
dot-com bubble fashion:</i>

15:56.831 --> 15:58.832
<i>by having an outrageous yacht party</i>

15:58.833 --> 16:00.417
<i>with lobster fights and hookers.</i>

16:00.418 --> 16:02.294
<i>We did Ecstasy,
which was terrible for you,</i>

16:02.295 --> 16:04.379
<i>and only ever made me feel fantastic.</i>

16:04.380 --> 16:06.214
<i>Kids, don't do it. It's too awesome.</i>

16:06.215 --> 16:08.550
<i>They said it would burn a hole
in your brain,</i>

16:08.551 --> 16:10.093
<i>- but show me the hole.
- Peter, that's enough.</i>

16:10.094 --> 16:12.262
<i>If you hate pure, unconditional love</i>

16:12.263 --> 16:14.723
<i>and experiencing the profound
harmony of the universe,</i>

16:14.724 --> 16:16.892
<i>definitely do not try this drug.</i>

16:16.893 --> 16:18.935
<i>There's also, like,
a 90% chance you'll hook up,</i>

16:18.936 --> 16:20.270
<i>but really, no, don't do it.</i>

16:20.271 --> 16:21.563
<i>Even if you don't hook up,
you don't care.</i>

16:21.564 --> 16:23.064
<i>But you'll hook up, guaranteed.</i>

16:23.065 --> 16:25.108
<i>Okay, Peter, let's move on.</i>

16:25.109 --> 16:27.110
<i>And what was the name of that drug?</i>

16:27.111 --> 16:28.403
<i>But despite our success,</i>

16:28.404 --> 16:30.614
<i>something was missing.</i>

16:30.615 --> 16:32.032
Peter, we did it!

16:32.033 --> 16:34.868
What's the matter?
You still sad about Brandon Lee?

16:34.869 --> 16:37.412
Yeah. I never heard of him
before he died,

16:37.413 --> 16:39.206
but when he died, it was so sad.

16:39.207 --> 16:40.960
But also, it's Lois.

16:40.961 --> 16:42.584
She's getting married tomorrow.

16:42.585 --> 16:45.045
Somehow, all this success
feels meaningless,

16:45.046 --> 16:46.796
knowing I'm about to lose her forever.

16:46.797 --> 16:48.632
Peter, then you need
to stop that wedding

16:48.633 --> 16:49.883
before it's too late.

16:49.884 --> 16:51.593
But we've got a business to run.

16:51.594 --> 16:53.428
You don't care about this business.

16:53.429 --> 16:55.472
All you've ever cared about is Lois.

16:55.473 --> 16:56.973
This is your last shot.

16:56.974 --> 16:59.309
Peter, you get to that wedding.

16:59.310 --> 17:00.727
<i>They were right.</i>

17:00.728 --> 17:02.229
<i>So I decided to get there</i>

17:02.230 --> 17:04.272
<i>the way everyone got around
in the '90s...</i>

17:04.273 --> 17:06.027
<i>Propelled by an explosion.</i>

17:12.114 --> 17:14.991
Do you, Lois
Commondenominator Pewterschmidt,

17:14.992 --> 17:18.287
accept this man to be
your lawfully wedded husband?

17:20.831 --> 17:23.500
Peter? What the hell
are you doing here?!

17:23.501 --> 17:26.002
Lois, can I talk to you privately?

17:28.089 --> 17:30.006
What is it, Peter?

17:30.007 --> 17:32.801
<i>Before you marry Tom, what's
the Mortal Kombat blood code?</i>

17:32.802 --> 17:34.177
I keep forgetting.

17:34.178 --> 17:37.597
It's "A-B-A-C-A-B-B,"
but you can't do this now!

17:37.598 --> 17:39.099
You're ruining my wedding!

17:39.100 --> 17:40.809
Lois, if I didn't come here,

17:40.810 --> 17:42.852
I'd regret it for the rest of my life.

17:42.853 --> 17:45.605
I know I screwed up,
and I don't deserve you,

17:45.606 --> 17:47.941
but I can't stop thinking
about you, day and night.

17:47.942 --> 17:50.277
It's been this way since the day we met.

17:50.278 --> 17:53.989
I fell in love with you then,
and I'll never stop.

17:53.990 --> 17:56.199
Unless Daisy Fuentes felt something?

17:56.200 --> 17:58.076
Uh, I didn't.

17:58.077 --> 17:59.703
Lois, you're the only woman for me.

17:59.704 --> 18:00.954
He cheated on you!

18:00.955 --> 18:03.123
No daughter of mine is going
to marry a cheater!

18:03.124 --> 18:04.499
Daddy's right.

18:04.500 --> 18:06.501
Peter, I'm sorry, but you blew it.

18:06.502 --> 18:10.046
I was in love with you, too,
but then you cheated on me.

18:10.047 --> 18:12.048
You kissed Daisy Fuentes.

18:12.049 --> 18:15.010
Lois, there's something you should know.

18:15.011 --> 18:17.846
<i>He didn't kiss me. I kissed him.</i>

18:17.847 --> 18:19.806
Because you felt something?

18:19.807 --> 18:21.349
Because Carter paid me.

18:21.350 --> 18:22.517
Well, that's something!

18:22.518 --> 18:24.894
Daddy... is that true?

18:24.895 --> 18:28.231
I only did it to protect you
from making a huge mistake!

18:28.232 --> 18:30.984
Lois, I may not be
as smart or as handsome

18:30.985 --> 18:33.153
as the guys your dad wants for you,

18:33.154 --> 18:36.031
but I love you more
than all of 'em put together.

18:36.032 --> 18:38.158
That's a fact. Just as sure

18:38.159 --> 18:41.411
<i>as the Star Wars movies are
a perfect isolated trilogy,</i>

18:41.412 --> 18:43.457
unmarred by additional canon.

18:43.458 --> 18:45.448
Oh, Peter!

18:48.419 --> 18:50.337
<i>- Damn it, stop them!
- One by one,</i>

18:50.338 --> 18:53.757
<i>members of Lois' family tried
to stop me, but I laid 'em out.</i>

18:53.758 --> 18:55.508
<i>There's something about punching someone</i>

18:55.509 --> 18:57.926
<i>in a church that just feels good.</i>

19:03.059 --> 19:05.894
<i>Cleveland picked us up
in a white Bronco.</i>

19:07.477 --> 19:09.939
Why did you have a white Bronco, Daddy?

19:09.940 --> 19:12.067
I was driving my innocent friend O.J.

19:12.068 --> 19:14.611
and his ex-wife's head down to Mexico.

19:14.612 --> 19:16.404
<i>We eloped at Fenway Park,</i>

19:16.405 --> 19:18.531
<i>which I paid 50 grand to rent out</i>

19:18.532 --> 19:20.660
<i>the day before the dot-com bubble burst.</i>

19:20.661 --> 19:25.081
I now pronounce this
the last straight marriage.

19:26.290 --> 19:27.832
<i>And I think</i>

19:27.833 --> 19:29.209
<i>I got swindled on the Fenway deal</i>

19:29.210 --> 19:30.877
<i>because there was a game that night.</i>

19:30.878 --> 19:33.254
<i>It's a hit!</i>

19:33.255 --> 19:36.383
<i>No! That would have been
the game-winning run!</i>

19:36.384 --> 19:38.343
<i>The Red Sox lose.</i>

19:38.344 --> 19:40.261
Boo!

19:40.262 --> 19:41.971
<i>I was having serious regrets</i>

19:41.972 --> 19:44.599
<i>about my decision, but was
already pregnant with Meg,</i>

19:44.600 --> 19:46.434
<i>so there was no backing out.</i>

19:46.435 --> 19:47.811
Boo!

19:50.481 --> 19:52.774
This bee's chasing me!
Somebody call Ace Ventura!

19:54.110 --> 19:55.945
Ow!

20:01.450 --> 20:02.910
<i>Aw.</i>

20:09.291 --> 20:12.585
Wow, Mom and Dad. I feel like
I learned so much tonight.

20:12.586 --> 20:15.505
And not just about you guys,
but also about the '90s.

20:15.506 --> 20:18.299
Oh, there's a lot more to learn
about the '90, Meg.

20:18.300 --> 20:20.009
Like, for instance, are you familiar

20:20.010 --> 20:21.761
with a band called "Counting Crows"?

20:21.762 --> 20:24.264
I think I might have heard them
in a Starbucks.

20:24.265 --> 20:25.849
Yes, you have.

20:25.850 --> 20:28.935
Anyway, their lead singer is
this thing called Adam Duritz.

20:28.936 --> 20:31.646
He looks like if Marc Maron
had sex with a scarecrow

20:31.647 --> 20:33.982
and gave birth to a baby made of hemp.

20:33.983 --> 20:36.317
I always thought
he looked like the Cowardly Lion

20:36.318 --> 20:39.195
<i>in a suburban white high school
production of The Wiz.</i>

20:39.196 --> 20:41.239
- That's not what that is?
- No, Chris.

20:41.240 --> 20:42.949
But actually, the joke's on us,

20:42.950 --> 20:45.493
because this Sideshow Bob burnout slept

20:45.494 --> 20:47.829
with a primo roster of '90s tail.

20:47.830 --> 20:49.664
- Jennifer Aniston.
- No.

20:49.665 --> 20:51.374
- Courteney Cox.
- What?!

20:51.375 --> 20:53.418
- Winona Ryder.
- That guy?!

20:53.419 --> 20:56.129
Christina Applegate,
Lara Flynn Boyle, Emmy Rossum.

20:56.130 --> 20:58.506
Ooh, this is just making me angry.

20:58.507 --> 21:01.969
- Mary-Louise Parker.
- I hear she's difficult.